---
{
  title: "substitute_tokens"
}
---
### NAME

    substitute_tokens() - Substitutes ${token} placeholders in a string with
    values from a mapping.

### SYNOPSIS

    string substitute_tokens( string text, mapping tokens );

### DESCRIPTION

    Substitutes ${token} placeholders in a string with values from a
    mapping.

    Keys are bare names, without the ${ } around them: a key of "mud_name"
    answers the placeholder ${mud_name}. Values may be of any type and are
    rendered through stringify(), so an int token needs no conversion at the
    call site.

    The whole string is resolved in a single pass, which is the point of
    doing this rather than a chain of replace_string() calls. A value that
    itself contains ${...} lands as literal text instead of being expanded
    by a later key, so this is safe to point at names and other text the mud
    did not write.

    A placeholder with no matching key is left where it is, so an unresolved
    token shows up in the output rather than silently becoming nothing.

### PARAMETERS

    text    (string)
            The text to substitute into.

    tokens  (mapping)
            Bare token names mapped to their values.

### RETURN VALUES

    (string) The text with every known placeholder replaced.

### ERRORS

    If text is not a string. If tokens is not a mapping.
